vcc_projector.h and vcc_projector.cpp in this directory are a C++ port of vcc/projector.py from

  hermes-vcc-engine
  https://github.com/danbiocchi/hermes-vcc-engine
  commit 31ee4fe7ef3e3f6c67dadfd45ebc1a3cb9773f95
  Copyright 2026 danbiocchi
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The upstream vcc/NOTICE reads (its second part, an MIT notice for Hermes Agent, is omitted: it
covers anchors.py, which is not ported):

  hermes-vcc-engine
  Copyright 2026 danbiocchi

  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Changes: ported to C++ for NInfer. Only the projector is ported (not engine.py or anchors.py, the
Hermes integration); the previous-summary merge, focus terms, session id and is_real_user filter
are left out, and the input is NInfer's ChatMessage mapped to the Hermes message shape (see
vcc_projector.h). The output is byte-identical to the Python projector at that commit on the
fixtures in tests/fixtures/vcc (tools/bench/vcc_golden.py). Those fixtures include conversions of
upstream tests/transcripts.py and tests/test_projector.py (same project, commit and license). vcc_unicode_tables.inc holds Python
3.12.3 (Unicode 15.0.0) character-class tables generated by that script.

